 "self_load_only": true,
 "description": "BIGVILLE R8 (block 256000) -- the DREAM layer (the ungrounded escape fantasy that makes a soul more than a utility function). gg_dream_ungrounded audits the dream onto the UNGROUNDED side of the grounding boundary (NO grounded_path edge, unlike a life-goal's path_to). gg_dream_relief (HEADLINE) is AFFECT REGULATION: when the present turns aversive (valence < aversive_threshold, driven there by R7 foreclosure/homeless distress) invoking the dream gives TEMPORARY relief (valence up by relief_valence, arousal down by relief_arousal, arousal floored at 0) WITHOUT touching any material attr (coin / balance / homeless UNCHANGED) -- the escape valve; ABLATE the dream (no has_dream edge) -> the identical aversive state has NO relief. gg_dream_collapse_threshold (valence <= collapse_threshold, present unbearable) and gg_dream_collapse_path (a recruiter minted a grounded_path -- a real path appears) COLLAPSE the dream into an actionable ActionGoal{kind:leave} (add_node) and the soul ACTS (left=1). gg_dream_latent is the CONTROL: below threshold + no path -> the dream stays LATENT (latent=1, resigned=1, left=0) -- resignation / the learned-helplessness floor (the abuse line). The three collapse/latent rules are DISJOINT (threshold: valence<=thr & no path; path: path present; latent: valence>thr & no path) so exactly one fires per collapse arm. Composes existing Terms; zero new Rust.",
